module.exports = /*#__PURE__*/JSON.parse('[{"id":1,"tip":"Not enough coffee","additionalInfo":"If you\'re not using enough ground coffee for the size of your portafilter basket, the brew time will be too quick. ","link":"https://www.rumblecoffee.com.au/blogs/coffee-brewing-guides/why-is-my-espresso-extracting-too-quickly#:~:text=GRIND%20SIZE,-There\'s%20two%20main&text=If%20your%20coffee%20beans%20are,down%20your%20espresso%20shot%20time."},{"id":2,"tip":"Your grind is too coarse","additionalInfo":"If your coffee beans are ground too coarse, the water can pass through the coffee grounds far too quickly, resulting in an under-extracted coffee. By grinding your coffee finer, it can resist the flow of the hot water more effectively, and slow down your espresso shot time.","link":"https://www.rumblecoffee.com.au/blogs/coffee-brewing-guides/why-is-my-espresso-extracting-too-quickly#:~:text=GRIND%20SIZE,-There\'s%20two%20main&text=If%20your%20coffee%20beans%20are,down%20your%20espresso%20shot%20time."},{"id":3,"tip":"Your tamp is too light","additionalInfo":"When your tamp is too light, it creates inconsistencies in the puck, causing channeling and for the water to run through too quickly.","link":"https://coffeebros.com/blogs/coffee/top-10-reasons-your-espresso-shot-pulls-too-slow-or-too-fast#s-b72ccc53-934c-4b0d-8bc5-b0752d33a7b8"},{"id":4,"tip":"Your temperature is too hot","additionalInfo":"The hotter the water, the quicker it is to extract compounds such as oils, acids, and caffeine. ","link":"https://www.coffeebean.com/blog/our-coffee/water-and-coffee-understanding-how-temperature-affects-your-cup"},{"id":5,"tip":"Too much coffee","additionalInfo":"If you overfill your machine with coffee, the water will take longer than it should to dispense through the grounds. ","link":"https://vdkrogt.com/2018/08/09/4-reasons-your-espresso-is-dispensing-too-slowly/"},{"id":6,"tip":"Your grind is too fine","additionalInfo":"If you grind your coffee too fine, the particles will fit too tightly together and prevent water from getting through at an adequate speed. ","link":"https://vdkrogt.com/2018/08/09/4-reasons-your-espresso-is-dispensing-too-slowly/"},{"id":7,"tip":"Your tamp is too hard","additionalInfo":"If your coffee is ground too fine, the water won\'t be able to get through which will cause your machine to choke and splutter.","link":"https://baristaandco.com/blogs/news/perfect-extraction-time-espresso"},{"id":8,"tip":"Your temperature is too low","additionalInfo":"When coffee is under-extracted, it can cause a sour taste and lack of body. This flavor profile occurs because the oils aren’t extracted, leaving the coffee without body or sweetness and bitterness to provide balance.","link":"https://www.coffeebean.com/blog/our-coffee/water-and-coffee-understanding-how-temperature-affects-your-cup"},{"id":10,"tip":"Your grind is the wrong size","additionalInfo":"if your shot takes longer than 25 seconds to pull your grind is too fine. If it takes less than 20 seconds to pull, then the grinds are too coarse.","link":"https://www.roastycoffee.com/no-crema-on-espresso/"},{"id":11,"tip":"Your beans are old","additionalInfo":"Stale coffee beans have been exposed to oxygen, thus breaking down the oils that give high-quality coffee its flavor.Without those oils, crema cannot be produced. ","link":"https://www.businessinsider.com/why-coffee-gets-stale-when-sitting-out-oxygenation-2015-9?r=MX&IR=T"},{"id":12,"tip":"Not enough pressure","additionalInfo":"Try tamping harder to increase the pressure.","link":"https://coffeeza.com/blogs/coffeeza-blog/why-does-my-espresso-have-no-crema#:~:text=In%20regular%20espresso%20machines%2C%20using,be%20finer%20than%20table%20salt."}]');

